/-!
# The map's general arguments, certified

A general argument on the map says that every model meeting some conditions has a verdict.
Here each verdict of an argument proved in Lean is one theorem, named
`Arguments.<argument id>.<principle id>` (a topic's argument, `arguments/<id>.yaml`) or
`Arguments.<group id>.<argument id>.<principle id>` (a group's shared argument), whose type is
the statement the map generates for it (`Classicism/ModelStatements.lean`):

- a topic's argument: for every intensional action model meeting the conditions, each the
  Lean predicate named in `conditions.yaml` (`Models/Conditions.lean`), the verdict;
- a group's argument: for every value of what the group's construction is built from (for the
  finite-support models on one object, a monoid acting faithfully on `ℕ`) meeting the group's
  conditions, the verdict in the model built from it.

A model then gets the argument's verdict by applying the certificate to its proofs of the
conditions: `MapDerived.lean`, generated by the map, for every model the map gives the argument.
-/

namespace Classicism.Map.Arguments

open CategoryTheory Meta Meta.Intensional Meta.Intensional.Premodel Meta.Intensional.MonoidModel

